Subject: [overlay 0042] when the shadow lights fit, admit them all — the cull is the over-cap path

Reported in the headset on 1.0.11.22 (rerelease data, base1, per-pixel lighting, VR): "Right at
the beginning of base1, at this wall, if I stand right in this spot it's LIGHT in my left eye,
DARK in my right eye. If I move to the left it's bright in both eyes, if I move to the right
it's dark in both eyes. This kind of thing is all over the place — walls, floors, etc."

0041 removed the SERVER's position cull (PHS against the light's own zero-size leaf) and put a
client-side relevance cull in its place: keep a light iff its bounding sphere touches a leaf in
the view leaf's PVS. Better question, same SHAPE of answer — a hard, position-dependent step.
And the q2repro per-pixel light shader has NO occlusion term: a light in the adjoining leaf
lights the near face of the thin wall between them, and the desktop reference shows that light,
because the PHS sent it. So a light the PVS test drops can still have been painting visible
pixels one step earlier. That is the both-eyes half of the report.

On base1 the cull is additionally doing no useful work. R18 measured it: 37 shadow lights
defined, all 37 sent every frame after 0041, the relevance cull admitting 24-33 of them
depending on where you stand, and ZERO evictions — the 64-slot MAX_DLIGHTS cap is never
reached. It was removing 4 to 13 lights the array had room for, at a position threshold.

WHAT THIS PATCH DOES

  A. CL_AddShadowLights becomes two passes. Pass 1 counts what the server sent this frame.
     If that count fits the budget, the frame runs in ADMIT-ALL mode: no relevance test at
     all, every sent light goes to V_AddLightEx. Only when the sent set exceeds the budget
     does 0041's cull run — which is what it should always have been, a way to choose what to
     lose when they cannot all be kept, not a permanent filter. 0041's code is untouched on
     that path (relevance, then the intensity x lightstyle x fade x proximity ranking at the
     cap).

  B. The budget is MAX_DLIGHTS minus the lights already in r_dlights minus a reserve of 8,
     via a new V_ShadowLightBudget() in view.c (r_numdlights and the slot bookkeeping live
     there, so the arithmetic does too). By the time CL_AddShadowLights runs, every transient
     effect light of the frame is ALREADY counted — CL_AddEntities calls CL_AddPacketEntities
     (muzzle flashes, item glows, rocket and BFG trails), CL_AddTEnts (explosions) and
     CL_AddDLights before it — so the subtraction is exact, not an estimate. The reserve
     covers LOC_AddLocationsToScene, the one V_AddLight caller that runs AFTER us (locs.c,
     under cl_drawlocs), plus headroom against a future stage being added after this one and
     silently starved. 8 of 64 is 12.5%: base1's 37 never come near it, and a map dense
     enough to need the cull path is exactly the map that gets it.

  C. The PVS row (V_UpdateShadowLightVis) is now decompressed only on the cull path — pure
     cost when nothing is going to be culled.

  D. SHADOWDIAG gains `mode=admit-all|cull budget=N`. The existing fields are unchanged and
     in the same order, so artifacts/vr-r18/analyze.py parses both builds. In admit-all mode
     `relevant` equals `sentbyserver` by construction (nothing is tested).

WHY THIS CANNOT BE THE PER-EYE HALF OF THE REPORT

The client's selection is EYE-INDEPENDENT, and this is worth stating because R19's second item
is the per-eye split. Every position input to the selection — V_ShadowLightRelevant's view
leaf, V_AddLightEx's fade and proximity — reads cl.refdef.vieworg at CL_AddShadowLights time,
and CL_AddShadowLights runs from CL_AddEntities, which runs after CL_CalcViewValues and BEFORE
view.c's per-eye pose injection. So cl.refdef.vieworg is the PRE-VR body origin at this point:
both eyes of a frame select the identical light set from the identical origin. R18 confirmed
it in the numbers (eyesplit 0/1816 publish pairs). A light lit in one eye and dark in the other
therefore arises downstream, in the refresh — that is diagnosed separately.

Nothing in the shader, the dlight mask, or 0031/0039/0040's stamp logic is touched. Upstream
defect, upstreamable as-is; a flat desktop takes the same path.

Apply: patch -p1 -d vendor/q2repro < this
--- a/src/client/client.h
+++ b/src/client/client.h
@@ -930,6 +930,9 @@
